WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.269 --> 00:00:11.200
The United Nations was founded 75 years ago&nbsp;to
save future generations from the scourge of war,

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.918
uphold human rights, and promote social&nbsp;
progress. The U.N. deserves credit for alleviating poverty,

00:00:16.918 --> 00:00:22.738
promoting human rights, and brokering peace&nbsp;
treaties. But a rising China and a revanchist Russia

00:00:22.738 --> 00:00:27.360
have been using the U.N. to promote their&nbsp;
own interests: shaping U.N. values and rules,

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.960
sometimes to the point of absurdity. Despite being&nbsp;
two of the leading countries responsible for human

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:39.120
rights violations, China and Russia have both just&nbsp;
been elected to the U.N.'s Human Rights Council.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.680
The U.N. is one of many arenas in which&nbsp;
the Trump administration's isolationism

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.394
has allowed China and Russia to expand&nbsp;
influence in international politics.

00:00:48.394 --> 00:00:55.920
China now leads four of 15 U.N. agencies, not to&nbsp;
mention its power over the WHO. To protect freedom

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:01.153
across the world, and to remain relevant, the U.N.
desperately needs to be reformed.

00:01:01.153 --> 00:01:07.259
The US must not allow Russia and China to reform the world.

00:01:07.259 --> 00:01:11.598
Do you&nbsp;think that the United Nations should be reformed?
Let us know in our poll.

00:01:11.598 --> 00:01:16.542
Also, let us know&nbsp;what other topics you'd like
our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:22.000
and be sure to LIKE and&nbsp;SUBSCRIBE
for more research and videos from AEI.

